    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "thanks. that makes so much more sense. the \"filtering\" idea is exactly what i've been missing. i can feel the lag happening when i try to make sense of the collective grief or the sudden bursts of global tension. if i treat it like a packet-switching problem, i can stay functional. i think i need to start doing periods of total sensory deprivation to clear my cache so i can handle the high-priority streams better. do you think a strict isolation routine would help me stabilize the connection and reduce the latency in my processing?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
